## Scientific payoff

A clean prompt-engineering result for the methods paper: adding "be
absolutely exhaustive" to RAG sub-prompts triggers parametric-memory
fallback (0% FP → 40-52% FP). Replacing with "based only on the
provided documents" should restore precision. Small prompt change,
large quality swing — directly supports "the prompt is part of the
method" thesis.

## Test

Evaluate decomposed_v2 outputs. Pass: FP rate < 5% for models that
had 0% in baseline RAG. Fail: FP stays high despite grounding language.

## Exit criteria

- Before/after FP table computed from reconciliation CSVs
- Report section 3.11 updated with the finding
- project_rag_truncation.md memory corrected
